{"additions":1302,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds a repository-local personal config: vig now reads a **gitignored-by-convention `.vig.kdl`** from the current worktree root and merges it on top of the user config, so one repository can get its own theme, pages, layouts, or keybindings (full user-config schema). Because a cloned repository may *ship* a committed `.vig.kdl`, trust is decided by git tracking: an **untracked** file (the user's own) loads silently, a **tracked** file (repo-provided) shows a **trust dialog** before the app is built — `[y]` load & remember, `[n]` ignore & remember, `[v]` view the file first, `Esc` ignore this time. Decisions are remembered in `$XDG_STATE_HOME/vig/trust.json` keyed by (worktree path, SHA-256 of the content), so a changed file asks again.\n\n![repo-config demo](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/td72/vig/feat/repo-local-config/assets/demo-repo-config.gif)\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Merge order** builtin → user → repo-local (`Config::with_repo_layer`, full validation re-run per layer so errors name the right file); `--config` / `$VIG_CONFIG` replace the user layer only\n- **Trust model** (`src/core/config/repo.rs`): tracked/untracked via `git ls-files --error-unmatch`; classification (`Absent` / `Disabled` / `Load` / `Declined` / `Undecided`) is a pure function with the git answer injected for tests\n- **Trust store** (`src/core/config/trust.rs`): JSON at `$XDG_STATE_HOME/vig/trust.json` (fallback `~/.local/state`); corrupt store degrades to empty; worktree keys normalized (git2 workdirs carry a trailing slash)\n- **Pre-app trust dialog** (`src/core/ui/trust_dialog.rs`): minimal self-contained event loop before `build_pages` (the answer decides which pages/keybindings exist); `v` opens a scrollable file viewer\n- **Kill switch**: `repo-config \"off\"` in the *user* config disables the layer and the dialog (default `\"on\"`, values validated)\n- **Graceful degradation**: repo-layer parse/validation errors never abort — vig starts with builtin + user, status bar shows `ignored .vig.kdl: <reason>` (one line on stderr too); user-config errors stay fail-fast\n- **CLI**: `vig config path` is now a three-layer listing (path + loaded / ignored + reason); new `vig config trust` / `vig config trust --forget <path>`; startup status bar shows `loaded .vig.kdl` once when the layer applied\n- **Docs**: layering + trust model in `docs/config.md`, short mentions in README / docs/README.ja.md\n- **Demo**: `tape/demo-repo-config.tape` + GIF (untracked silent load, `vig config path`, trust dialog with `v` → `y`, `vig config trust`), `mise run demo:repo-config` wired into `demo:all`\n- **Tests** (17 new): layer precedence, kill switch, tracked/untracked classification, trust store roundtrip / hash invalidation / corrupt file / forget, error degradation, `config path` status texts\n\n## Not verified\n\n- The trust dialog was exercised via the VHS recording (tracked repo → dialog → `v` → `y` → app starts with the layer), not by an automated TTY test\n- `$XDG_STATE_HOME` unset fallback (`~/.local/state`) is covered by code/tests but the manual smoke test ran with `$XDG_STATE_HOME` set\n\nCloses #132\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":16,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T06:27:34Z","deletions":80,"headRefName":"feat/repo-local-config","labels":[],"number":138,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdG2EQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe current implementation has a trust-bypass failure mode (when `git` tracking detection fails) and a couple of correctness/perf issues that should be addressed before merging.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nAdds a repository-local configuration layer (`.vig.kdl`) that can override the user config on a per-repo basis, gated by a pre-app trust dialog when the file is git-tracked, with persisted decisions in an XDG state JSON store.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Introduces repo-local config discovery/merge (builtin → user → repo-local) plus a `repo-config \"on|off\"` kill switch.\n- Adds trust classification + persisted trust decisions (`trust.json`) and new CLI subcommands (`vig config path` layer listing, `vig config trust [--forget]`).\n- Adds a pre-app trust dialog UI (including a scrollable “view file” mode) and updates docs + demo tape/GIF.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tape/demo-repo-config.tape | VHS demo covering untracked auto-load and tracked trust dialog flows |\r\n| src/main.rs | Wires repo-layer application before app build; adds `config path` layer listing and `config trust` |\r\n| src/core/ui/trust_dialog.rs | Implements pre-app trust dialog + scrollable viewer |\r\n| src/core/ui/mod.rs | Exposes `trust_dialog` module |\r\n| src/core/config/trust.rs | Trust store model + JSON persistence + timestamp formatting |\r\n| src/core/config/repo.rs | Repo-layer discovery/classification, tracking check, apply/summary/status helpers |\r\n| src/core/config/mod.rs | Registers new `repo` and `trust` config modules |\r\n| src/core/config/merge.rs | Adds `repo-config` to merge rules/top-level validation |\r\n| src/core/config/loader.rs | Adds repo-layer merge API + validation refactor + `repo_config()` getter |\r\n| README.md | Mentions repo-local `.vig.kdl` and trust dialog at a high level |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese README mention of repo-local `.vig.kdl` and trust model |\r\n| docs/config.md | Documents layer order, trust model, commands, and `repo-config` |\r\n| mise.toml | Adds demo task and includes it in `demo:all` |\r\n| Cargo.toml | Adds `sha2` dependency for content hashing |\r\n| Cargo.lock | Locks `sha2` dependency |\r\n| assets/demo-repo-config.gif | Adds demo GIF (LFS pointer) |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 15/16 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 4\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T06:31:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"a52dccdca12f90da41cf86ade3c75b612a03fa82"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdITRA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe trust store currently overwrites prior decisions per worktree (undermining the documented per-content-hash trust model) and the trust dialog has a couple of edge-case correctness issues (small-terminal viewer sizing and large-line-count truncation).\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**src/core/ui/trust_dialog.rs:144**\n* In the viewer, `view_area` uses `.max(20)` / `.max(6)` for width/height. On small terminals this can produce a `Rect` that extends beyond `area` (e.g., width becomes 20 even when the terminal is narrower), which can cause rendering glitches or panics depending on backend assumptions. Clamp the viewer size to the available area (use `saturating_sub` only, like the other dialogs).\n```\n    let margin_x = area.width / 10;\n    let margin_y = area.height / 10;\n    let view_area = Rect::new(\n        margin_x,\n        margin_y,\n        area.width.saturating_sub(margin_x * 2).max(20),\n        area.height.saturating_sub(margin_y * 2).max(6),\n    );\n```\n**src/core/config/trust.rs:206**\n* If `TrustStore::remember()` is adjusted to keep decisions per (worktree, hash), this unit test should be updated accordingly. As written, it asserts that remembering a new hash removes the old hash decision, which re-prompts the user if the `.vig.kdl` content ever reverts to a previously-trusted version.\n```\n    fn changed_hash_invalidates_decision() {\n        let mut store = TrustStore::default();\n        store.remember(Path::new(\"/w/a\"), \"oldhash\", TrustDecision::Load);\n        assert_eq!(store.decision(Path::new(\"/w/a\"), \"newhash\"), None);\n        // A fresh decision replaces the stale entry instead of piling up.\n        store.remember(Path::new(\"/w/a\"), \"newhash\", TrustDecision::Ignore);\n        assert_eq!(store.entries.len(), 1);\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 15/16 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 3\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T06:35:28Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"a52dccdca12f90da41cf86ade3c75b612a03fa82"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdRo-A","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThere are confirmed correctness issues in `vig config trust --forget` key matching and in the trust dialog viewer sizing that can break behavior on real systems.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 15/16 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:00:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"e64767c84f681d0056147f48a95375088e3704a3"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdcIHQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:24:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"e64767c84f681d0056147f48a95375088e3704a3"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdcIqw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:25:00Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"e64767c84f681d0056147f48a95375088e3704a3"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdegNg","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d8f5fc3541ccf52bcbb953153614f8a24deb7f5c"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdeg7A","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:33Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d8f5fc3541ccf52bcbb953153614f8a24deb7f5c"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdeh2Q","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d8f5fc3541ccf52bcbb953153614f8a24deb7f5c"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdeibw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:36Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d8f5fc3541ccf52bcbb953153614f8a24deb7f5c"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdejMQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:37Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d8f5fc3541ccf52bcbb953153614f8a24deb7f5c"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdekCg","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d8f5fc3541ccf52bcbb953153614f8a24deb7f5c"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdekvg","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:40Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d8f5fc3541ccf52bcbb953153614f8a24deb7f5c"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdgelg","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nThe startup status message for `.vig.kdl` is set via `AppContext.status_message` but isn’t cleared automatically, so the “once at startup” notice can persist and obscure normal status-bar content indefinitely.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (3)\n\n**Previously missed (2)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**src/main.rs:292**\n* `startup_notice` is stored in `AppContext.status_message`, but there’s no mechanism to auto-clear status messages. As a result, `loaded .vig.kdl` / `ignored .vig.kdl: …` will persist indefinitely and keep replacing the normal status-bar content (e.g. git file/stats, files selection info), which contradicts the PR description of showing it “once at startup”. Consider adding a one-shot/TTL mechanism (e.g. clear on the first key press or after the first tick/draw) so regular status content returns automatically.\n```\n    let ctx = AppContext {\n        should_quit: false,\n        active_page: 0,\n        page_labels,\n        page_keys: Vec::new(),\n        show_help: false,\n        status_message: startup_notice,\n        error_dialog: None,\n        workdir: workdir.clone(),\n        needs_full_redraw: false,\n    };\n```\n**src/core/ui/trust_dialog.rs:87**\n* The dialog/help text doesn’t mention all supported keys: the code treats `q` as equivalent to `Esc` (and `Ctrl+c` as ignore) but the prompt only advertises `Esc`. This makes the UI instructions inaccurate and hides available escape hatches.\n\nThis issue also appears on line 170 of the same file.\n```\nfn render_dialog(f: &mut Frame, area: Rect, path: &Path) {\n    let message = vec![\n        \"This repository ships a tracked .vig.kdl:\".to_string(),\n        String::new(),\n        format!(\"  {}\", path.display()),\n        String::new(),\n        \"It is a full vig config (pages, layouts, keybindings)\".to_string(),\n        \"provided by the repository, not by you.\".to_string(),\n        String::new(),\n        \"[y] load and remember    [n] ignore and remember\".to_string(),\n        \"[v] view the file        [Esc] ignore this time\".to_string(),\n    ];\n```\n\n**src/core/ui/trust_dialog.rs:176**\n* In the viewer footer, the help text says `Esc back`, but the handler also supports `q` to exit the viewer. Updating the footer avoids confusing users who try `q` and makes the key hints consistent with behavior.\n```\n    let block = Block::default()\n        .borders(Borders::ALL)\n        .border_style(Style::default().fg(ACCENT).bg(BG))\n        .style(Style::default().bg(BG))\n        .title(format!(\" {} \", path.display()))\n        .title_bottom(\" j/k scroll · y load · n ignore · Esc back \");\n    f.render_widget(\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 15/16 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:34:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d8f5fc3541ccf52bcbb953153614f8a24deb7f5c"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T08:34:06Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33373511219/job/99429731361","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-31T08:34:14Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:02Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33368546724/job/99414268920","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:28:51Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:29:20Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33368546708/job/99414268706","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:28:50Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:29:46Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33368546724/job/99414268591","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:28:52Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:42Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33368546724/job/99414268828","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:28:50Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:42Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33368546724/job/99414698002","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:42Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T08:34:06Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33373511219/job/99429699952","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-08-31T08:34:07Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:29:36Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33368546708/job/99414268962","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:28:50Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:22Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33368546708/job/99414268806","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:28:50Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T08:34:06Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33373511219/job/99429700627","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-08-31T08:34:07Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"✨ Repository-local personal config (.vig.kdl) with a trust dialog"}
